{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/26851-making-vampires-scary","id":26851,"title":"Making Vampires Scary","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-09T17:38:01-08:00","id":26851,"title":"Making Vampires Scary","content":"This could well be a result of my ST skills, but whenever I run a Hunter game the characters tend to approach the supernatural as kind of ho-hum, easy to deal with. Hit vampires with improvised flamethrowers, werewolves with shotguns, and so on, which according to the rules really does kind of, and I apologise for the language but I cannot think of an alternative that really captures my meaning, f<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">uc</span>k the supernaturals s<span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">hi</span>t up (slight censoring to avoid offense).<br /> <br /> Apart from changing the rules (say vampires aren't vulnerable to fire, or whatever), what are some ways that can make vampires and the other supernatural creatures scary? Even if I changed their weakness, then the players would just adjust to capturing one, then testing out until they found it, then it'd be the same thing. More dice for the enemy doesn't seem to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T17:53:57-08:00","id":26860,"title":"","content":"There's both a pre-combat and in-combat answer here.<br /> <br /> Precombat; it should take your players an <b>age</b> to even figure out that they're dealing with a Vampire. Don't tell them &quot;There's a Vampire that hangs out at Club Goth; go get it!&quot; but let them come across <i>something</i> and then try and figure out what it is - there's this guy who's always at the Club, stays real late, and always leaves with the prettiest girl in the bar.... actually now that he thinks of it the bartender never sees them come back. He never buys his own drink, either.... All the while the Vampire can be gathering intel on <b>them.</b><br /> <br /> Both Vampires and Werewolves are acutely aware of their own weaknesses; this means they can plan for the worst. Vampires can live in buildings with fire systems; put those flamethrowers out! (Actually they have it even better than that; Kindred don't need to breath so very very well connected Vampires could have an <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inergen\" target=\"_blank\">Inergen</a> or <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Halomethane\" target=\"_blank\">Halon</a> fire suppression systems which both put out the fires, <b>and</b> make an environment that people who need to actually breath in find very toxic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Werewolves are BIG and FAST and SCARY; if they're fighting against people using silver shotguns (because real shotguns only cause Lethal, and Werewolves are totally capable of shrugging that off, or healing it quickly at least), they can get out before it gets nasty. And being able to hide themselves as normal people means they'll be much harder to find again.<br /> <br /> A couple of quick thoughts, hope they helped <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/568-viperion","name":"Viperion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar568_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T18:04:02-08:00","id":26865,"title":"","content":"I feel the direct combat threat isn't what makes vampires scary at all. Sure, they go down like punks to a improv flamethrower. But few vampires want to go toe to toe with an enemy that is ready for them and, crucially, knows they're a vampire. A vampire with Auspex and Obfuscate is a master of hiding, stalking and striking from the shadows. Nightmare and Obfuscate adds the ability to creep people out with literal hallucinations, split them up and take 'em down. That's two clans right there being terrifying.<br /> <br /> Maybe attempt a less visceral horror? The vampire will be easy to kill, sure, but he's got the police on side. Capable, armed ghouls .A devoted cult that, oops, your sister just joined (and she's got a nasty Vitae addiction). You killed a vampire? His friend is angry at you. And he'll come for you, but first he'll use his friends at city hall and the police station to make your life a misery before you're dragged into a police cell due to planted evidence, framed for a crime you didn't commit, and you're unarmed... and that's when he emerges, grinning, from the shadows.<br /> <br /> So, got for the Alien approach - stealth in combat - and a more conspiracy horror feel. Nothing worse than bringing some ghouls along - it's psychologically nasty and they don't have the vampire allergies to sunlight and fire (though, to be fair, people tend to be pretty hurt when you set them alight). Go for family members and loved ones. Play up that the vampire is<i> not alone</i> and has allies amongst its own kind and among people.<br /> <br /> And try to hide that the vampire is, well, a vampire. One using Protean, especially under Blood and Smoke rules, could appear utterly inhuman, with lots of tiny insect-limbs, a bladed tail, a snake's distended jaws... Vampires might appear, or claim to be, gorgons, werewolves, mummies, zombies, horned demons (I can name bloodlines, clans and NPCs for these)... And if you really wanna have some fun by playing on alternate vampires pick up <i>Night Horrors: The Wicked Dead</i> and encounter some of the weird vampires from mythology and the minds of the White Wolf writers.<br /> <br /> Frankly, in a straight fight next to nothing is scary, and if it's immune to everything it's scary for a second, then <i>annoying</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 07-17-2016, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T18:40:20-08:00","id":26888,"title":"","content":"Use the monster creator rules and some of the advice sections to craft vampires that aren't as obvious and easy to counter for someone who's seen vampire movies.<br /> <br /> It's not changing the rules.<br /> <br /> There's a vampire in VtR who can walk around in the sun freely. There's a werewolf who can punch someone with a dice pool around 40. There's changelings that drink blood and other changelings who can look like werewolves, and Prometheans can look like werewolves, and you can simply use Hunter's monster creation stuff to make literally any sort of monster that won't be easily slain by someone who's watched a horror movie and can apparently easily capture monsters more powerful than humans. Again for the changeling thing, they can turn any portal into a gateway to the hedge if they can touch it, so taking one around or putting them in a cage can just bring the hunters into a world of hurt. Any of those can make a promethean that is like them enough to pique interest but they can ignore the traditional vulnerabilities. And any of those can be concerned that their friends have been taken by a bunch of murderhobos who have pierced their carefully concealed lifestyle hiding behind the Masquerade, and use their influence to find out where they live and start systematically ruining their lives or simply pop up in the hunters' bedrooms in the middle of the night and explain to them what a dangerous lifestyle they've chosen for themselves. <br /> <br /> If you stick to standard opponents, you can expect standard responses to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 12-09-2013, 10:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T07:30:52-08:00","id":27966,"title":"","content":"It's already been mentioned, but it bears repeating. Just because it comes out at night and drinks blood doesn't make it a vampire, and not all vampires have to hide during the day and drink from humans. Here's a short list of other creatures who drink blood:<br /> <br /> Alan<br /> Chupacabra<br /> Gaki<br /> Golden Hind<br /> Kappa<br /> Kekkai<br /> Lamia<br /> Manananggal<br /> Redcap<br /> Rokurokubi<br /> Sigbin<br /> Vulkodlak<br /> Yuki-onna<br /> <br /> You wanna scare a hunter, throw something new at them. Something that a wooden stake in the chest would just piss off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T08:49:24-08:00","id":28003,"title":"","content":"Oh come off it, Alan's not that bad.<br /> <br /> Chortle chortle snort snort gawd I'm <i>SO</i> funny.*dies in a corner alone*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T09:56:02-08:00","id":28062,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget the <a href=\"http://bogleech.com/yaramayhawho.html\" target=\"_blank\">Yara-ma-yha-who</a>, a rare daylight-only vampire-ish being (eats and regurgitates you a few times before you turn). It's silly, but there <i>is</i> a lot of potential there.<br /> <br /> (Actually, a vampire who may well have been the origin of this myth is mentioned in Clanbook Gangrel)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Onyx Path Freelancer: Demon Storyteller's Guide, Dark Eras, Night Horrors: Enemy Action</i><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/825063-storyteller-s-guide-extra-material\" target=\"_blank\">Storyteller's Guide Extra Material</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/899423-after-the-fall-bonus-material\" target=\"_blank\">After the Fall: Bonus Material</a>","edited":{"userid":452,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","user":"Eremite","date":". 12-11-2013, 12:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/452-eremite","name":"Eremite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar452_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-13T16:10:02-08:00","id":29593,"title":"","content":"Some good suggestions, many thanks guys/girls <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T21:42:56-08:00","id":48712,"title":"","content":"You show up with flamethrowers and stakes. The vampire isn't there. The vampire isn't there because she's busy blood-bonding your mom, eating your kids, foreclosing on your house, and having your car towed. Someone <i>is</i> here, though. It's the Fire Marshall and his police escort, here to do a routine inspection of the property at the request of the owner (the nice pale lady who always calls at night). They're very interested in why a ragtag group of social misfits with spotty employment histories and possible criminal records have just committed B&amp;E while carrying an illegal and frankly absurd array of weapons. Okay, to be perfectly honest, they're not actually interested in why.<br /> <br /> Later, when you're all alone and unarmed in a jail cell, she'll consider obfuscating her way in and finishing the job. She'll make it look like a suicide. The neighbors will all confirm that you had a history of erratic behaviour and antisocial tendencies. And, I mean, you kicked in the door of a house in a good neighborhood and threatened city employees with <i>flamethrowers </i>and <i>stakes,</i> like they were goddamn <i>vampires</i> or something. You were <i>clearly</i> crazy. No one will question it.<br /> <br /> The trick is not to play supernaturals as D&amp;D monsters who basically stand around doing nothing until the adventurers show up, and then leap straight into combat. Instead, play them as people. Specifically people who want to stay alive, and who have been doing this, successfully, a lot longer than the hunters have. These people have been playing the supernatural game longer, they know more, and they are better positioned to use that knowledge. Unless the hunters are incredibly discreet, their target probably sees them coming, and isn't going to wait around to fight them fair and square. Fair and square fights are not how you survive. And even a vampire caught with her pants down isn't going to fight to the death against a fire-wielding hunter squad: she's going to get the fuck out of there, lick her wounds, and then come at the cell <i>hard</i> in ways they're not prepared to cope with. And bear in mind, she probably has friends, or at least other dead people who owe her favors.<br /> <br /> If all else fails, ask yourself: if this were a Requiem game, and I was playing this vampire as a PC, and this group of hunters was coming for <i>my character</i>, how would I turn the tables on them and make them regret their decision to survive infancy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 01-14-2014, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T22:20:00-07:00","id":932408,"title":"","content":"The above is a perfect description. Vampires are a lot like humans. Raw strength isn't their greatest asset, regardless of what powers they have. The reason they've survived so long and spread so far is that they're sneaky, creative bastards (though given how buffed they got in B+S, they're still a pain head to head).<br /> <br /> Another idea to play with- see if you can make your players start to wonder if every vampire they killed died because another vampire wanted him dead. Make them wonder, &quot;Maybe we're only killing the dumb and careless ones...and maybe the smart ones got us to do it for them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I would also agree that you should vary things up, throwing some weird stuff at your players, other vampiric creatures or things that aren't what they appear, etc. But you should also never forget that you can make canon, baseline, as-written Kindred absolutely terrifying to even the most powerful and well-equipped Cell.<br /> <br /> Even at Conspiracy level, what I said about uncertainty very much applies: Mister White has an agreement with The Company. A gentleman of his stature in the community has many enemies, and he can't be bothered to deal with them all himself. So he makes sure The Company knows just enough to take them down, and in return none of the acquisition personnel employed by The Company will ever even know that Mister White exists. That is, unless they start asking questions. And we all know where questions get you in The Company. Or someone more powerful than Mister White makes a better offer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 07-16-2016, 01:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T15:31:26-07:00","id":932654,"title":"","content":"In the words of Robin, the Boy Wonder:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i171.photobucket.com/albums/u286/xxbluespade2xx/Thread-necro.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T20:23:49-07:00","id":932761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/26851-making-vampires-scary?p=932654#post932654\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the words of Robin, the Boy Wonder:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"http://i171.photobucket.com/albums/u286/xxbluespade2xx/Thread-necro.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div> I, for one, approve of thread necromancy; it keeps a conversation going, so no one has to answer a question 4 times because people keep making new threads with the same questions over and over.<br /> <br /> So, your Hunter cell kicks in the door of Neonate Kenny's liar. 10 minutes later, Kenny's dead, but so is half your cell; turns out the liar was also a meth lab, and your improvised flamethrowers set fire to more than just vampires. It gets worse; Kenny was working on a way to make Vitae infused meth, on the orders of an Ordo Dracul Elder, who wanted to see if that would be a more efficient way to create blood addicts. Now that Elder is pissed at you and your cell for fucking up his experiment.(he doesn't give a shit about Kenny) Oh, did I forget to mention this Elder is the head of the biggest crime family in the Tristate Area?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp