ntent":"So what I'm getting is that there's two &quot;levels&quot; of vampire society: there's the ones who do their own feeding and hunting at clubs and such, the lower strata, &quot;low hanging fruit&quot; as it were. But there's another level: the elders. They have people brought to them, or dedicated blood dolls/servants. And they're much harder to track, but they do watch the youngers, mostly for two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. They're their main competition for power in vampire society.<br /> <br /> 2. Because they're low-hanging fruit, they can serve as a kind of &quot;early warning&quot; system for hunters. Any go missing unexpectedly, and something's probably up. Might be another elder making some kind of play, but might also be hunters (or of course, both). Either way, a response of some kind is warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}